*Heading
crack_tip_fields FE case study (2D plane strain): Fe single crystal, Bunge (27, 0, 0)
**
** Boundary-layer model for the K-field check (manuscript, Section 4).
** Units: mm, N, MPa. Crack tip at the origin, crack along the negative x-axis up to the
** outer radius R = 1 mm; the crack faces are a seam (crack-face nodes exist twice).
** Mesh: 5184 CPE8 elements, 15715 nodes (identical in all 2D cases); the elements at the crack tip are
**   collapsed quadrilaterals, their mid-side nodes on the edges at the tip sit at the quarter point (t = 0.25).
** Material:
**   Fe, C11/C12/C44 = 243.36/145.01/116.04 GPa, rotated with Bunge (27, 0, 0)
**   (stiffness rotated into the global system with rotate_stiffness_euler of crack_tip_fields.py)
** Load: displacements of the analytical crack-tip field, K_I = 27.5 MPa sqrt(m) = 869.626 MPa sqrt(mm),
**   a = 1 mm, on the outer boundary; file Fe_27_0_0_mode_I_bc.inp written by abaqus_crack_tip_bc_app.ipynb
**   (anisotropic, material 'Fe (cubic, example)', Euler (27, 0, 0)).
** Output: J-integral on 6 contours around the tip; K_I = 2 sqrt(J/E22), see evaluate_kfield_abaqus.py.
**
** Sets: BULK          all elements
**       BOUNDARY      nodes of the outer boundary (r = R, incl. both crack-face nodes)
**       CRACK_FRONT, CRACK_TIP   crack-tip node (contour integral)
**
